The cast — persona files and artwork
===================================

Copyright (c) 2026 Art Pai. All rights reserved, except as granted below.

The maids of Claude Café — their names, their persona files (`*/persona.*.md`)
and their artwork (`*/expressions/`, `*/portraits/`) — are the identity of this
project rather than part of its source code, and the MIT license at the
repository root does not cover them.


You are welcome to
------------------

- Put any maid to work with Claude Code: hire her from claudecafe.dev, keep her
  persona in `~/.claude/cafe/personas/`, and let her serve you.
- Change her for your own use — rewrite her lines, redraw her, dress her
  differently — as long as the result stays something you use rather than
  something you publish.
- Quote her and screenshot her when writing about the project.


Please don't
------------

- Sell her, or anything derived from her.
- Publish her as your own character, or under a name that would leave people
  believing your version is the one from Claude Café.
- Use her name or her face to suggest this project endorses something it
  doesn't.


About the artwork, honestly
---------------------------

The sprites and portraits were generated with AI image tools, from pencil
references and a written style spec kept outside this repository, then finished
with the scripts under `scripts/`. How much copyright attaches to work made that
way is unsettled, and the answer differs by country — in some of them it is
little or nothing.

So take the rules above for what they are: a request about how to treat someone
else's work, not a threat. The persona files are a different matter — they are
written text, and protected as such.
